.page-section.p-120-cont.cg-section.grey-light-bg.clearfix(id="problem-link")
    .container
        .row
            .col-md-10.col-md-offset-1.text-center.mb-60
                h2.cg-section-title Most scaling systems fail in the same 3 ways
        .row.cg-problem-grid
            .col-md-4
                .cg-feature-card.wow.fadeIn
                    .cg-feature-icon
                        .icon.icon-ecommerce-graph1
                    h3 AWS costs outpace value
                    p Monthly cloud spend grows with traffic while architecture stays unchanged. Waste hides in Lambda configuration, API Gateway, data transfer, and idle capacity.
            .col-md-4
                .cg-feature-card.wow.fadeIn(data-wow-delay='150ms')
                    .cg-feature-icon
                        .icon.icon-basic-bolt
                    h3 APIs degrade under real load
                    p Latency spikes, timeouts, and flaky dependencies show up in production—not in demos. Hot paths in Go services, queues, and databases need engineering, not more instances.
            .col-md-4
                .cg-feature-card.wow.fadeIn(data-wow-delay='300ms')
                    .cg-feature-icon
                        .icon.icon-basic-lock
                    h3 Legacy architecture slows shipping
                    p Monoliths and manual ops block safe deploys. Teams want event-driven, serverless boundaries so they can release often without overnight maintenance windows.
